<title>UK: RM and Virgin plan internet education service.</title>
<headline>RM and Virgin plan internet education service.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>RM Plc said on Monday it has agreed with Virgin Net, a joint venture between Virgin Communications and CableTel, to provide an education service to home users via the Internet.</p>
<p>Virgin Net, 51 percent owned by Richard Branson's Virgin Group with the remainder held by US cable firm International CableTel Inc, is expected to launch a new internet service in early November.</p>
<p>RM, which supplies information technology solutions to educational markets, said it plans to make the RM service available next year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
